al features and when he first saw  him yoshitaru thought that Alba was a  girl Alba is a botanist who actually  discovered the legendary blue Spider  Lily that muzan had been trying to  locate for his entire life apparently  the blue Spider Lily only blooms during  the day for two or three days a year so  it was extremely difficult to find and  yet after going through all that trouble  of finding and researching this  extremely rare flower someone in the  research team made a mistake and all of  the flowers withered after that the  research program came under intense  criticism and Alba lost his job he met  sumihiko one day when they were both  crying in the same park and the two of  them became friends they like to play  badminton together Alba also has one  little brother but the brother does not  appear in the story  tengiruzui has a descendant by the name  of Tenma uzui Tenma is a 20 year old  gold medalist in gymnastics he is known  for having a flashy attitude and for  doing things like giving the middle  finger to the camera and choking  reporters who tried to follow him around  he also has seven siblings our boy guiyu  has a descendant as well his name is  gichi tomioka and he is an elementary  school student the butterfly estate  girls have descendants and they are just  normal schoolgirls the swordsmith hotaru  haganezuka also has descendants and  there is a maintenance store in modern  Tokyo called haganezuka maintenance  kotetsu kanamori goto and Takeuchi also  have descendants as does murata murata's  descendant is a school principal who  tries to close the school gate before  sumihiko and tojiro can get in but they  still manage to get to class on time by  just hopping over the fence and speaking  of tojuro that is when things get  interesting not all characters that we  see in modern day Tokyo are descendants  of the original characters some of the  characters in chapter 205 who look and  act almost exactly like the characters  we know from the taisho period cannot be  descendants of The Originals because the  original characters never had children  if we accept the words of sumihiko and  kanata's grandmother and yoshitaru's  words as well then we can assume that  those characters are not descendants but  reincarnations of those who died in  battle while fighting muzon and the  demons those who sacrificed their lives  to defeat muzon have been reincarnated  into a happier life in the modern world  and this was foreshadowed multiple times  throughout the course of the series  these reincarnations include muichiro  tokito and his brother yuichiro who have  been reincarnated into the modern world  as twin babies we also have shinobu and  kanae who have been reincarnated as  regular high school girls that yoshitaru  is clearly attracted to gyome has been  reincarnated as a kindergarten teacher  which suits his character and backstory  perfectly best girl mitsuri and iguro  have been reincarnated as a married  couple who operate a diner together the  diner is known for its snake decorations  and massive portion sizes which is a  hint that mitsuri niguros still have the  same personalities as they did in their  former lives mitsurian iguro also have  five children together Kanata says that  he can't show his face at that  restaurant anymore because the last time  they went yoshitaru kept staring at  mitsuri's big chest and iguro ended up  throwing a knife at them because  yoshitaru wouldn't stop staring zenitu  Sensei giguro was also reincarnated but  even in the modern world he is already  an old man and he looks almost exactly  as he did before he also enjoys playing  shogi sabito and makomo have been  reincarnated as elementary school kids  and they are best friends with gyu's  descendant gichi in the extra pages that  were included with the final volume of  the manga it is revealed that yorichi  and his wife and child were also  reincarnated into a happier life but now  let's get back to tojoro and also let's  talk about genya and sanami because  sometimes the line between modern day  descendants can be become a bit blurry  so for example tojoro is confirmed to be  the descendant of senjuro kyojiro  rengoku's younger brother but at the  same time he has an almost identical  personality to kyojro himself and it is  heavily implied that he is indeed The  Reincarnation of kyojiro since kyojiro  also died in battle against the demon it  would only make sense for him to also be  reincarnated and it seems that he was  reincarnated as his brother's descendant  in terms of sanami he has a modern day  descendant who became a police officer  this descendant has a partner who is  like a brother to him and this partner  seems to be The Reincarnation of genya  it appears that these two guys used to  be delinquents and they actually got  into a fight with each other and scarred  each other's faces with knives then they  were arrested together and eventually  they became friends turned their lives  around and became cops finally there are  a couple of characters from the original  story who are still alive in the modern  world yushiro is still alive because he  is a demon and he hasn't aged he has  become a famous artist known for  creating beautiful paintings of a woman  who looks a lot like Tamayo he has  recently gained International Acclaim  but he is a very private individual and  he is rumored to even shoot at reporters  who tried to interview him this makes  sense since the more people learn about  yushiro the more likely they are to  figure out that he doesn't age the cat  chachamaru is also still alive and still  living with yushiro due to the fact that  you should have turned the cat into a  demon before the battle against muzan  finally kiria ubyashiki the son of  kagaya ubayashiki is also still alive  but he is not alive due to some sort of  demonic power he is simply really old  and in fact he is currently the oldest  living person in Japan he is presumably  over 108 years old at this time and he  is still friends with yushiro and those  are all the details that we get about  the time skip in the Final Chapter and  the extra pages there is no doubt in my  mind that the mangakau of Demon Slayer  koyoharu kotoke fully intended to leave  things as is after the Epic defeat of  muzon demons were no longer a threat the  demons are core disbanded and everyone  lived happily ever after that was  certainly the original plan however  after the manga ended in May of 2020  Demon Slayer continued to absolutely  blow up in popularity Mugen train became  the highest grossing Japanese film of  all time and the highest grossing film  of 2020 with over half a billion in  earnings despite the fact that he was  released during a pandemic the Demon  Slayer manga would also go on to become  by far the best-selling manga of 2020.  Demon Slayer sold over 82 million copies  in 2020 alone which was literally 10  times more than the second best-selling  manga Kingdom even in 2021 long long  after the Demon Slayer manga ended demon  Slayers still sold almost 30 million  copies despite ending the year before  Demon Slayer was still the second  best-selling manga after the still  ongoing Jujutsu Kaizen manga which sold  only about a million more copies than  Demon Slayer now I'm not mentioning  these numbers just to brag about how  popular Demon Slayer is I am mentioning  these numbers because shuisha the  publisher of Demon Slayer will be  extremely motivated to continue the  manga in some way because there is just  so much money to be made here even if  kotoke fully intended to end the manga  completely in 2020 the explosion in  popularity and profitability of the  demon sire franchise changes the game  the publisher will definitely try to get  gotorege to continue Demon Slayer either  with a sequel a prequel or a spin-off  that takes place in the same world and  even if godogue doesn't want to continue  the story herself there is always the  option of having another manga take over  as was the case with Dragon Ball super  and boruto knowing how this industry  works I would be more surprised if there  wasn't some sort of continuation to the  story than if there was I mean it is  possible for kotoke to just say no I  don't need any more money and I don't  want to continue the story in any way  but that just doesn't seem like a likely  scenario I mean Kishimoto didn't really  need any more money either and yet  boruto still happened in fact Demon  Slayer has already released some extra  chapters that were created by authors  other than gotoke for instance the  rangoku and giyu Gaiden chapters were  written and illustrated by another  mangaka called hirano ryoji but if there  is a continuation to the story what kind  of continuation would it be there are  multiple options including a prequel  series that takes place during yorichi's  lifetime if this prequel happened it  would feature a pretty amazing cast  including yorichi kokushibo Tamayo muzan  then of course tanjiro's ancestor  sumioshi because of this I think that if  a prequel ever happens this is the most  likely period that it would be set in we  could also get a spin-off which takes  place in the same world but focuses on  other characters while potentially  featuring occasional appearances by  characters from the original so this  would mean new Heroes new demon villains  and new settings to explore either other  parts of Japan or maybe even other  countries the good thing about a  potential spin-off is that this would  allow for almost complete freedom to  whoever is writing it since that person  doesn't need to directly impact the main  story that said a spin-off that doesn't  focus on the characters that we know and  love could end up being a lot less  popular and thus less profitable the  final option is a sequel which would  either take place in the modern world  after the time skip or during the time  skip itself if the sequel were to take  place in the modern world then it would  focus on The Descendants and  reincarnations of the original  characters  featuring of course yushiro and the cat  but if the sequel were to take place  during the time skip so sometime after  the defeat of muzan and before the  modern era then theoretically we could  have the main characters that we know  and love be the focus of the story  although they would be somewhat older  this latter option allows us to see how  strong characters like inosuke zenitsu  and tanjiro could become as adults and  it would also allow us to witness the  rise of a new generation of hashira but  again this scenario would clearly have  to account for the fact that gotoke  wasn't planning on continuing the story  of tanjiro and the Gang for one thing as  I said earlier the Demon's air core was  disbanded because it was no longer  necessary after muzan's defeat in order  for the Demon's air core to be formed  once again a new demon threat would have  to emerge since yushiro survived all the  way up to the modern era we know that  muzan's death did not automatically kill  off every other demon so technically it  is possible that there are more demons  hiding out there somewhere and because  we now know that the blue Spider Lily  does still exist it is also possible  that new demons could be created in the  same way that demon muzan was himself  created one thousand years ago that said  there would need to be a good  justification for why this major new  demon threat was never mentioned in the  original story is this an ancient demon  who was turned by muzon hundreds of  years ago and maybe had a falling out  with muzon at some point in the past did  this demon maybe flee to another country  to escape muzan's wrath but then decide  to return after muzan's death I do think  that there's a way to make this work but  it has to be handled with care another  thing that a potential sequel featuring  the original characters would have to  account for are tanjiro's pretty severe  and debilitating injuries as a result of  his fight with muzan tanjiro lost the  use of one arm and one eye which is the  same type of injury that led tang and  Uzi to retire from being a hashira  because he didn't think that he could  fight effectively with such injuries so  if tanjiro is to become a hashira the  son hashira who uses hinokami kagura  then he has to find a way to fight  despite his injuries tanjiro is  extremely determined so I'm sure that  there is a way to make this work but it  certainly won't be easy other than just  training really hard in order to learn  to fight with only one hand and one eye  another option could be to have nezuko  fighting alongside him so for example  nezuku and tanjiro could decide to start  training together for years until they  learn to overcome each other's  shortcomings in battle and so then the  two of them together could become the  son hashira kind of like daki and yutaro  together were upper Moon six I mean  Demon Slayer is full of these types of  deliberate parallels between the heroes  and villains so I could definitely see  it happening however there could also be  more like cheat code ways of healing  tanjiro for example yushiro could use  tamayo's research to come up with a cure  for tanjiro's injuries or maybe some of  muzon cells within tanjiro could  reactivate and regenerate his body at  some point in the future in chapter 203  when tanjiro breaks free of muzan's grip  and wakes up we don't actually see muzon  cells disintegrate muzan just screams at  tanjiro not to leave him there but we  don't see his cells melting or  disappearing or anything like that so  who knows but again while it is possible  to make tanjiro the Sun hashira as part  of a potential sequel it would have to  be handled with care okay so let's  assume that all of this happens a new  demon threat appears years after the  defeat of muzon and the demon Slayers  are reassembled let's say that tanjiro  is now capable of fighting again and  that the hashira ranks are also being  re-established tanjiro or tanjiro and  nezuko together are given the title of  but who would the other hashira be in  this new Demon Slayer organization we  could expect guiyu and sonami to stay on  as the water and wind hashira provided  at the curse of the Demon Slayer Mark  doesn't kill them by age 25. since the  ubayashiki curse was clearly broken  after muzan's death and since yorichi  was able to live into his 80s we can  assume that it is indeed possible to  break the curse of the Demon Slayer Mark  and if all else fails you should all  just make some magical potion or  something and we're good zenitude then  becomes the Thunder hashira inosuke  becomes the Beast hashirath kanal  becomes the flower hashira and since  this is taking place years after the  defeat of muzon are now older senjuro  can succeed his brother as the flame  hashira that makes seven hashira and I  don't think that we necessarily need  nine hashira but if we wanted to fill  the other two positions maybe two new  characters could fill fill those spots  alternatively we could have older and  stronger versions of established  characters like kiria aoi or murata take  the spot and if you need to ask yes  murata would of course be the goat  hashira because he is the goat so to  reiterate I think that some sort of  Demon Slayer story continuation is  extremely likely because the series is  just so incredibly profitable the only  questions are what form this  continuation would take and how involved  the original mangakagotolege would  actually be the continuation could be a  prequel a spin-off or a sequel and all  of them could be really good if they are  handled the right way and if some  serious thought is put into the plot and  character development definitely let me  know down in the comments if you want to  see the Demon Slayer story continue in  some way and if so what type of  continuation do you want to see most  prequels spin-off sequel during in the  time skip sequels set in modern times  also who do you think would be the next  generation of hashira if the Demon's air  core were to be re-established after the  defeat of muzan don't forget to leave  your thoughts down in the comments below  I hope you guys enjoyed this video and I  hope that I was able to clearly and  effectively explain the time Skip and  all that stuff about descendants and  reincarnations don't forget to leave a  quick like it only takes a second but it  helps a lot and of course if you're new  here or maybe you watch our videos but  you just haven't taken the time to  subscribe yet do me a quick favor and  make this the video that you subscribe  and hit that notification Bell to turn  on all notifications you can also hit me  up on Twitter and Instagram at anime  offroar don't forget to check out  itaikuji and use the promo code anime  Pro 500 link down below as always thank  you guys so much for watching and until  next time time see ya Space Cowboys
 

